course: dictionary
lesson: 15372
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word spa is a good example. «The old town grew up around the spa, where warm water bubbled out of the ground.» The clue is the warm water from the ground, so a spa is a place with natural springs.
explain: «Mum booked a spa day for her birthday, with a massage and a swim.» Now the clues are massage and swim, so a spa here is a place where people go to relax with treatments. Always ask: what is happening here, and where? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A spa is a place with natural mineral water springs, where people drink or bathe in the water to feel healthier.
fact: A spa town is a town that grew up around such springs, like Bath in England.
fact: A spa day means a day of relaxing treatments, such as massages, saunas and pools.
fact: In the USA, Australia and New Zealand, a spa often means a small hot tub with bubbling water.
fact: The plural of spa is spas, so «There are three spas in the town» is correct.
exercise: «The children visited the old spa town, where warm water bubbled from the ground.» What is a spa town? | *A town that grew up around natural springs | A town with the biggest shopping centre | A town by the sea with no water at all | A town where a sports race is held every year
exercise: «Mum booked a spa day with a massage and a sauna.» What is a spa day? | A day spent cleaning the house | A day of running races | A day at school with extra lessons | *A day of relaxing treatments
exercise: «In Australia, Dad sat in the spa with bubbles all around him.» In Australia, what does spa often mean here? | A kind of shoe | *A hot tub at a house or hotel | A farm for animals | A long, old road
test: «The water from the spa was said to make people feel healthier.» What does spa mean in this sentence? | A kind of sports ground | A type of tree | A bowl for washing dishes | *A place with natural mineral water springs
test: Ella says spa only means a hot tub. Why is she only partly right? | *It can mean a hot tub in some countries, but also a place with natural springs or relaxing treatments | It means a kind of bread | It is a school subject | It always means a hot tub, in every country
exam: Read this: «The spa town was busy all summer.» What does spa town mean? | *A town that grew up around natural springs | A town with no water | Any town that has a school | A town that sells only hot drinks
